  "question_stem": "The displacement of a particle moving in a straight line is $s$ metres at time $t$ seconds after leaving a fixed point $O$. The particle starts from rest and passes through points $P$, $Q$ and $R$, at times $t = 5$, $t = 10$ and $t = 15$ respectively, and returns to $O$ at time $t = 20$. The distances $OP$, $OQ$ and $OR$ are $50$ m, $150$ m and $200$ m respectively.\n\nThe diagram shows a displacement-time graph which models the motion of the particle from $t = 0$ to $t = 20$. The graph consists of two curved segments $AB$ and $CD$ and two straight line segments $BC$ and $DE$.",
